{
  "manufacturer": "SmartGen",
  "manufacturer_slug": "smartgen",
  "model": "HGM7100N Series",
  "model_slug": "hgm7100n",
  "short_model": "HGM7100N",
  "aliases": [
    "HGM7110N",
    "HGM7120N"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Generator controller",
  "applies_to": "HGM7110N (auto start) and HGM7120N (AMF) genset controllers, protocol document v1.3.",
  "summary": "SmartGen's HGM7100N controllers run a single genset (HGM7110N) or a genset with automatic mains failure transfer (HGM7120N). The RS485 port is a Modbus RTU slave: alarms, modes and I/O are packed bit words, measurements and counters are 16-bit holding registers (FC03), and front-panel keys are mirrored as FC05 coils. This map covers the status and alarm words, frequencies, currents, power factor, battery voltage, state codes, counters, clock and the remote command coils; values without a printed scale and all 32-bit values are left out (see notes).",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "0-based",
    "note": "The appendix prints decimal addresses 0000-0284 and they are used as the wire address. Two examples confirm it: the FC05 example writes coil 0000 (Remote Start) at 0x0000, and the FC06 example writes 00E3H (= 227, Controller Time day) inside the FC06-writable range 0225-0231."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "HGM7100N Genset Controller Communication Protocol",
    "doc_number": null,
    "revision_date": "2025-06-21 (v1.3)",
    "url": "https://www.smartgen.cn/yun/data/download/HGM7100N_Protocol_en.pdf",
    "pages": "pp. 4-11 (frame format, function codes, examples), 12-25 (FC03/FC06 data field), 25-26 (FC05 coils), 26-27 (status tables)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "The document prints no units at all. Units are kept only where the document prints a multiplier ((*10) or (*100)) and the quantity name fixes the unit: frequency (Hz), phase current (A), battery and charger voltage (V); plus registers whose name states hour, minute or second. (*10) means the raw value is ten times the real value (scale 0.1), (*100) means scale 0.01.",
    "Left out because no scale or unit is printed: mains and gen phase and line voltages (0055-0060, 0075-0080), voltage phase angles (0061-0063, 0081-0083), load percentage (0140), engine speed (0141), the analog sensor values and resistances (0148-0157), the ECU-only J1939 values (0162-0170) and the state delay values (0190, 0192, 0194, 0196).",
    "Left out: all 4-byte values (per-phase and total kW, kvar and kVA at 0103-0126, current energy, average and historical power at 0134-0139, total fuel at 0171-0172, total kWh/kvarh/kVAh at 0203-0208 and the MCU ID). The document never states which register of a pair holds the high word, so the word order cannot be established from it.",
    "Bit words list bit 0 (LSB) first; reserved bits are omitted from the bit lists.",
    "FC06 is accepted only at 0199-0210 (run-time, start and energy counters) and 0225-0231 (clock); every other register is read-only. Of the writable counters only the 16-bit ones are mapped."
  ],
